-- How each pre-system society's figures were arrived at.
--
-- These eight were commissioned before this system existed and there was no
-- single method between them: one agreement extrapolates the demo's MEASURED
-- daily figure to the contracted count, the next uses the theoretical; one
-- averages two demos' percentages, another was billed on an annexure that
-- says outright it would be revised and never was; one starts billing the day
-- after installation completes, another the same day.
--
-- None of it can be corrected — it is what was signed and what these
-- societies have been billed on — so it is recorded instead, against the rows
-- the figures live on rather than in a spreadsheet nobody opens. A number
-- whose basis is unstated cannot be defended when it is questioned, which is
-- what INV-02 exists to prevent. New deals follow one method; these carry
-- their own, in writing, wherever the figure is shown.
--
-- Written by scripts/make-data-migrations.py from docs/backfill/*.csv, and
-- generated inline for every society imported after this one. Guarded so it
-- only ever fills a record that is still absent.

UPDATE circuits SET eligibility_checklist = eligibility_checklist
  || jsonb_build_object('deviations', '["eligibility-never-assessed", "dates-inferred-from-readings", "represented-count-from-invoice", "benchmark-single-demo", "benchmark-rounded-in-agreement"]'::jsonb, 'basisNote', 'Report''s own tables average to 48.6987 and 16.3629 -> 66.3998%, matching its stated figures exactly. Neither date is stated: meter-install taken as the day before its first reading (03 Aug), replacement as the day before the post-install readings start (16 Oct). NOTE - the meter workbook for this circuit shows consumption dropping from ~48 to ~18 kWh/day on 18 Aug 2025, so the lights were physically changed then; the report simply re-measured in October. Represented count is the first invoice''s own figure ("Number of lights = 2,508"), which the agreement rounds to 2,500.')
 WHERE id = 'bf-ace-city-ckt-1' AND NOT (eligibility_checklist ? 'deviations');

