UPDATE agreements SET deviation_note = 'Commissioned before this system existed. There was no single method across these societies, so how this deal''s figures were arrived at is recorded here rather than assumed. Departures from the standard: extrapolation-theoretical, fee-device-charge-plus-share-of-net, billing-starts-on-completion-day, report-share-differs-from-agreement. SOURCE IS THE USER''S PASTED TEXT (2026-08-28), not a file on disk - both the agreement and the demo report were supplied inline, so the readings below are transcribed from that text rather than parsed from a document. Every figure was checked against the documents'' own arithmetic and all of it reconciles exactly. Agreement made 07 Oct 2025, notarised and signed the same day 05 Feb 2026; billing from 15 Mar 2026: the first invoice was raised on 31 Mar 2026 for 17 days, and 17 days ending the 31st can only start on the 15th. Installation finished ON 15 Mar (the user, 2026-08-28), so billing began the SAME day it completed rather than the day after - a departure from CON-22''s normal rule, and the reason this contract''s term starts on the 15th rather than the 16th. Nothing here stores a completion date for CON-22 to derive from; term_start is taken as given. That first invoice is therefore prorated to Rs 6,546.65 ex-GST; the Rs 11,938 recorded here is the full monthly charge the contract runs at, which CON-22 prorates for the opening month. 400 lights agreed and 400 installed, so no additional-light charge applies. PRE-INSTALLATION CONSUMPTION IS THE THEORETICAL, NOT THE MEASURED, unlike ATS Greens Paradiso: 5,760 kWh/month is 400 x 20W x 24h x 30, where extrapolating the demo''s measured 23.80 kWh/day over 47 lights would give 6,076.6. The agreement took the lower figure, and every downstream number follows from it: 67.10% of 5,760 = 3,865 kWh at Rs 6.50 = Rs 25,122, less Rs 8,000 for hardware = Rs 17,122 net, of which FirsThing takes 23% = Rs 3,938, for a monthly payable of Rs 11,938 + GST. The structure is a fixed device charge plus a share of what remains, as at Amrapali Princely Estate, and reduces to a constant 47.5201% to FirsThing - 52.4799% to the society. Tolerance +/-10%, stated in the agreement''s clause 18 rather than defaulted. The demo report''s own ''50% of these verified savings'' does not match the agreement and is not used.'
 WHERE id = 'bf-bestech-park-view-residency-agreement' AND deviation_note IS NULL;
